WEBVTT

00:03.920 --> 00:04.320
All right.

00:04.320 --> 00:06.960
So with that we have a clear understanding what our views.

00:06.960 --> 00:09.960
But now you might ask me why do we need views.

00:09.960 --> 00:14.840
That's why now what we're going to do, we're going to deep dive into multiple scenarios and use cases

00:14.840 --> 00:17.440
that you might encounter in your SQL projects.

00:17.480 --> 00:22.680
So let's start with the first use case, the first use case, and the core reason why we use views in

00:22.680 --> 00:30.080
our data projects is to store central logic from a complex query in the database so that everyone can

00:30.080 --> 00:30.960
access it.

00:30.960 --> 00:36.680
And with that, we improve reusability between multiple queries, and we reduce as well the complexity

00:36.680 --> 00:38.280
of the overall projects.

00:38.280 --> 00:39.960
So let's understand what this means.

00:39.960 --> 00:44.200
So now in our project we have like two tables in the database orders and customers.

00:44.200 --> 00:49.440
And we have learned previously that if we have like a complex query we can go and use the CTE.

00:49.480 --> 00:54.640
So for example, in our city we are joining tables and doing some aggregations using the sum.

00:54.640 --> 00:57.600
And the city can store the data in an intermediate result.

00:57.600 --> 00:59.120
And then we have the main query.

00:59.120 --> 01:03.160
For example we are doing the step two where we are ranking the data.

01:03.160 --> 01:05.120
So the whole thing is in one query.

01:05.120 --> 01:09.360
And let's say that a financial analyst was doing this type of analysis.

01:09.400 --> 01:15.240
Now, what could happen is that you might have another user, for example, a budget analyst, where

01:15.240 --> 01:17.680
he is doing exactly the same first step.

01:17.680 --> 01:23.680
So he has as well a city query where first the data are joined and then aggregated using the sum.

01:23.680 --> 01:28.920
But the last step in the main query he is not doing ranking, he is just doing like max and min.

01:28.920 --> 01:35.120
And not only that, we have a third user, the risk analyst, where as well doing the same initial step

01:35.160 --> 01:39.000
using the CTE, joining the tables and doing the summarization.

01:39.000 --> 01:44.200
But here the risk analysis in this scenario is just comparing the data at the last step in the main

01:44.200 --> 01:44.760
query.

01:44.760 --> 01:48.560
So now if you sit back and look to this, you can see all the three data workers.

01:48.600 --> 01:51.080
All of them are doing the same first step.

01:51.080 --> 01:53.040
So all of them are doing the same CTE.

01:53.080 --> 01:55.920
They are joining the data and then doing summarization.

01:55.920 --> 02:01.560
And of course, this is a complete waste of time that each one of them has to create first the CTE from

02:01.560 --> 02:04.040
the scratch in order to do some analysis.

02:04.040 --> 02:06.880
So it is complete redundancy and makes no sense.

02:06.880 --> 02:11.360
So this is exactly the disadvantage of only using CTE in the projects.

02:11.440 --> 02:12.440
Now what we can do.

02:12.480 --> 02:16.760
Instead of that, though, three data workers can decide to say, you know what?

02:16.800 --> 02:20.480
Let's put the first step as a view in the database.

02:20.480 --> 02:26.120
So instead of using CTE, each time we're going to take this script and put it in the database.

02:26.120 --> 02:31.920
So we have now a central logic that is stored in the database where everyone can use it.

02:31.920 --> 02:37.080
So we have this query, this logic only once and everyone can benefit from it.

02:37.080 --> 02:43.440
So now the financial analyst, instead of going directly to the physical tables they can go to the view.

02:43.440 --> 02:47.640
So that means she needs only to write one script the rank scripts.

02:47.680 --> 02:49.600
Same thing goes for the budget analyst.

02:49.600 --> 02:54.640
He has only to write the query for the max and min and as well for the risk analyst, he just needs

02:54.640 --> 02:55.680
to compare the data.

02:55.680 --> 03:00.800
So as you can see, all those queries are reduced and they can only focus on the analyses.

03:00.800 --> 03:04.640
So this is exactly the magic of views in data analytics.

03:04.640 --> 03:08.360
This logic, this knowledge can be centralized in the database.

03:08.360 --> 03:14.960
And this is way faster and better than having this logic written each time someone wants to do an analysis.

03:14.960 --> 03:18.000
So this is why we need views in data projects.
